*.pyc
.pytest_cache/

# Build artefacts, not state. Both are regenerated on every run and uploaded to
# Pages from the working tree, so the deployed site always has them; committing
# them would add megabytes of churn and, worse, leave a stale copy in the
# repository that looks current. Anything the pipeline needs to *remember*
# between runs -- history.json, predictions.json -- is committed, and is not here.
site/og/
site/cal/
